// Benchmark 4 (`docs/rfc.md` §7.8): Veil/Quint-style fenced distributed lease handover under partitions.
//! explore: 2
Fact node Identified by Primary, Backup.
Fact coordinator Identified by Coord.
Fact active-lease Identified by node.
Fact epoch-fenced Identified by node.

Power grant-initial-lease Actor coordinator Recipient node
  Holds when !(Exists node': active-lease(node'))
  Valid when !(Exists node': active-lease(node'))
  Creates active-lease(node).

Act confirm-fence Actor node
  Holds when active-lease(node)
  Creates epoch-fenced(node)
  Terminates active-lease(node).

Power activate-successor Actor coordinator Recipient node
  Holds when (Exists node': epoch-fenced(node') && node' != node) && !(Exists node'': active-lease(node''))
  Valid when (Exists node': epoch-fenced(node') && node' != node) && !(Exists node'': active-lease(node''))
  Creates active-lease(node).

Invariant single-authority When !(Exists node, node': node != node' && active-lease(node) && active-lease(node')).
Property bounded-handover-safety When WeakUntil(single-authority(), False).

grant-initial-lease(Coord, Primary).

Scenario fenced-handover-preserves-single-authority {
  ?!valid activate-successor(Coord, Backup).
  confirm-fence(Primary).
  ?valid activate-successor(Coord, Backup).
  activate-successor(Coord, Backup).
  ?active-lease(Backup).
  ?!active-lease(Primary).
}
